## Formal Invention Description

### Title  
**Curable Vinylidene Fluoride Fluoroelastomer Composition Having Controlled End-Group Content and Limited Metal Hydroxide Loading**

### Field of the Invention  
The invention relates to curable fluoroelastomer compositions based on vinylidene fluoride-containing polymers. More particularly, the invention concerns peroxide-curable or coagent-curable vinylidene fluoride fluoroelastomer compositions having defined polymer end-group constraints and containing a limited amount of metal hydroxide, expressed in parts by weight per hundred parts by weight of fluoroelastomer rubber, or phr.

### Summary of the Invention  
Provided is a curable fluoroelastomer composition comprising:

1. **100 parts by weight of a vinylidene fluoride-containing fluoroelastomer**, the fluoroelastomer comprising recurring units derived from vinylidene fluoride and at least one additional fluorinated comonomer;

2. **a curing system** capable of crosslinking the fluoroelastomer, preferably a peroxide curing system comprising an organic peroxide and, optionally, a multifunctional unsaturated coagent;

3. **a metal hydroxide**, present in an amount of greater than 0 phr and not more than 10 phr, preferably from 0.1 to 8 phr, more preferably from 0.2 to 5 phr, based on 100 parts by weight of the fluoroelastomer; and

4. optionally, one or more fillers, processing aids, pigments, acid acceptors, stabilizers, or other conventional fluoroelastomer compounding ingredients.

The vinylidene fluoride fluoroelastomer is characterized by controlled end-group chemistry. In particular, the fluoroelastomer contains cure-reactive halogen-containing end groups, preferably iodine-containing and/or bromine-containing end groups, in an amount effective to participate in peroxide curing, while the amount of unstable or highly polar end groups is limited. In one embodiment, the combined concentration of acid fluoride, carboxylic acid, carboxylate, ester, hydroxyl, and other non-halogen polar end groups is not greater than 100 mmol/kg of polymer, preferably not greater than 50 mmol/kg, and more preferably not greater than 25 mmol/kg. In another embodiment, the fluoroelastomer contains terminal iodine and/or bromine atoms in a total amount of from 0.01 to 1.5 wt.%, preferably from 0.03 to 1.0 wt.%, based on the weight of the fluoroelastomer.

### Detailed Description  

#### Fluoroelastomer  
The fluoroelastomer comprises vinylidene fluoride units. Suitable fluoroelastomers include copolymers, terpolymers, and higher interpolymers comprising units derived from vinylidene fluoride and one or more fluorinated comonomers selected from, for example:

- hexafluoropropylene;
- tetrafluoroethylene;
- chlorotrifluoroethylene;
- perfluoroalkyl vinyl ethers;
- perfluoroalkoxy vinyl ethers;
- fluorinated olefins; and
- mixtures thereof.

In one embodiment, the fluoroelastomer comprises recurring units derived from vinylidene fluoride and hexafluoropropylene. In another embodiment, the fluoroelastomer comprises recurring units derived from vinylidene fluoride, hexafluoropropylene, and tetrafluoroethylene.

The vinylidene fluoride content may suitably be from 20 to 85 mol%, preferably from 35 to 80 mol%, and more preferably from 45 to 75 mol%, based on total monomer units in the fluoroelastomer.

#### End-Group Constraints  
The fluoroelastomer is selected or prepared so as to have controlled end-group functionality. In preferred embodiments, the fluoroelastomer includes halogenated cure-site end groups capable of participating in peroxide crosslinking. Such end groups may comprise iodine, bromine, or both.

In one embodiment, the fluoroelastomer satisfies at least one of the following end-group constraints:

- total iodine and/or bromine end-group content: **0.01 to 1.5 wt.%**, preferably **0.03 to 1.0 wt.%**, based on fluoroelastomer weight;
- total iodine and/or bromine end-group concentration: **0.1 to 50 mmol/kg**, preferably **0.5 to 25 mmol/kg**;
- combined concentration of non-halogen polar end groups, including —COF, —COOH, —COOR, —CH₂OH, carboxylate salt, and related oxidized end groups: **not more than 100 mmol/kg**, preferably **not more than 50 mmol/kg**, more preferably **not more than 25 mmol/kg**;
- substantial absence of thermally unstable end groups that generate excessive gas, acid, or chain scission products during curing or post-curing.

The end groups may be introduced by use of an iodine- or bromine-containing chain-transfer agent during polymerization, including, for example, diiodinated or dibrominated compounds, iodoperfluoroalkanes, bromoperfluoroalkanes, or compounds containing both iodine and bromine.

#### Curing System  
The composition preferably contains a peroxide curing system. Suitable organic peroxides include dialkyl peroxides, peroxy ketals, peroxy esters, and diperoxides. Examples include:

- 2,5-dimethyl-2,5-di-tert-butylperoxyhexane;
- dicumyl peroxide;
- di-tert-butyl peroxide;
- benzoyl peroxide;
- 1,1-di-tert-butylperoxy-3,3,5-trimethylcyclohexane; and
- mixtures thereof.

The organic peroxide may be present in an amount of from 0.1 to 10 phr, preferably from 0.5 to 5 phr.

The curing system may further include a coagent. Suitable coagents include triallyl isocyanurate, triallyl cyanurate, trimethallyl isocyanurate, triallyl trimellitate, N,N′-m-phenylene bismaleimide, and multifunctional acrylates or methacrylates. The coagent may be present in an amount of from 0.1 to 15 phr, preferably from 0.5 to 8 phr.

#### Metal Hydroxide  
The composition includes a metal hydroxide in a limited amount. The metal hydroxide may function as an acid acceptor, stabilizer, cure modifier, or processing aid.

Suitable metal hydroxides include:

- calcium hydroxide;
- magnesium hydroxide;
- barium hydroxide;
- strontium hydroxide;
- aluminum hydroxide;
- hydrotalcite-type hydroxides;
- mixed metal hydroxides; and
- combinations thereof.

The metal hydroxide is present in an amount of **greater than 0 phr and not more than 10 phr**, preferably **0.1 to 8 phr**, more preferably **0.2 to 5 phr**, and still more preferably **0.5 to 3 phr**, based on 100 parts by weight of fluoroelastomer.

In one embodiment, the composition excludes metal hydroxide loadings greater than 10 phr. In another embodiment, the composition excludes metal hydroxide loadings greater than 5 phr. The limited metal hydroxide content provides sufficient acid neutralization while reducing adverse effects such as excessive modulus increase, compression-set degradation, scorch, reduced elongation, or impairment of cure uniformity.

#### Optional Ingredients  
The composition may further comprise one or more optional additives, including:

- carbon black;
- silica;
- fluoropolymer micropowder;
- mineral fillers;
- processing aids;
- waxes;
- plasticizers;
- pigments;
- antioxidants;
- adhesion promoters;
- metal oxides;
- acid acceptors other than metal hydroxides; and
- release agents.

When present, fillers may be included in amounts from 1 to 100 phr, preferably from 5 to 60 phr.

#### Preparation  
The composition may be prepared by mixing the fluoroelastomer, curing system, metal hydroxide, and optional ingredients using conventional rubber compounding equipment, including an internal mixer, open roll mill, kneader, or twin-screw mixer. The organic peroxide is preferably added at a temperature below its significant decomposition temperature.

The compounded composition may be shaped by extrusion, molding, calendering, transfer molding, injection molding, or compression molding. The shaped article may be cured at a temperature of from 120°C to 220°C, preferably from 150°C to 200°C, followed optionally by post-curing at from 150°C to 260°C.

### Articles  
The composition is useful for forming cured fluoroelastomer articles including:

- O-rings;
- gaskets;
- seals;
- shaft seals;
- valve stem seals;
- hoses;
- diaphragms;
- tubing;
- fuel-system components;
- chemical-processing seals;
- semiconductor-processing seals; and
- automotive or aerospace elastomeric components.

### Exemplary Claim-Style Description  
A curable fluoroelastomer composition comprising:

- 100 parts by weight of a vinylidene fluoride-containing fluoroelastomer comprising recurring units derived from vinylidene fluoride and at least one fluorinated comonomer;
- an organic peroxide curing agent;
- optionally, a multifunctional unsaturated coagent; and
- a metal hydroxide in an amount of greater than 0 phr and not more than 10 phr;

wherein the fluoroelastomer comprises iodine-containing and/or bromine-containing terminal groups in an amount effective to provide peroxide curability, and wherein a combined amount of non-halogen polar end groups selected from acid fluoride, carboxylic acid, carboxylate, ester, and hydroxyl end groups is not greater than 100 mmol/kg of fluoroelastomer.

### Advantage  
The described composition provides a curable vinylidene fluoride fluoroelastomer having improved cure response, controlled processing behavior, and desirable cured physical properties while limiting the amount of metal hydroxide to avoid excessive stiffness, poor elongation, or compression-set deterioration.

The invention pertains to a fluoroelastomer composition comprising:

(a) a vinylidene fluoride (VDF)-based fluoroelastomer;

(b) at least one polyhydroxylated curing agent;

(c) at least one accelerant for promoting cure of the fluoroelastomer;

(d) at least one metal oxide; and

(e) optionally, at least one metal hydroxide.
